FINAL ANSWER:
Hybrid search integrates dense vector embeddings with sparse lexical keyword matching (BM25) using Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF). While vector search captures semantic nuances and synonyms, it frequently misses exact alphanumeric codes, acronyms, or rare product identifiers. Hybrid search ensures maximum recall and lexical precision across technical and enterprise domains.

