FINAL ANSWER:
ColPali is a Vision-Language Model (VLM) architecture that indexes document pages directly as visual images, bypassing brittle OCR text extraction and arbitrary chunking. By computing multi-vector patch embeddings with ColBERT-style late interaction, ColPali accurately retrieves information embedded in complex visual layouts, multi-column tables, charts, and diagrams that traditional text-only RAG pipelines typically lose.

